oplog 1008: PumpTick (median 826 ms) and MotorAccessPollTick (median 702 ms) passes use about 20 ms tick-thread CPU -- waiting, not computing.
Pci1203IoThreadRunSync now times its wait (QPC) and hands it to g_W906IoWaitHook (Pci1203Monitor.cpp EOF); wb_serve's pass profiler adds it
to the phase it happened in: "<phase> N ms (io wait W ms/count)". New phases: Pump: heater/DTME08/TemperFrom, St02Timers,
FlushFlag/DoorLock/Fan, MainProc, CounterRefresh; ServiceOutputs; MAPoll: core, Brake/BootInit/ParamSync, OverlaySnapshot, Hooks,
TorqueFocus. Measurement only, no behaviour change. WORKLOG row 212 + section 3 row for designer tools 0173 (d646730).

Debug + release wb_serve built; test_pci1203_pure 109/109, WB_SimPump passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
